# XSH abort()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.abort.001
anchor     functions/abort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A child calling abort() with SIGABRT at SIG_DFL does not return from
           it, and wait() reports termination by SIGABRT.
test       t/001-terminates.c

assertion  XSH.abort.002
anchor     functions/abort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A child that blocks SIGABRT, and another that ignores it, are each
           terminated by SIGABRT when they call abort().
test       t/002-blocked-ignored.c

assertion  XSH.abort.003
anchor     functions/abort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A child with a SIGABRT handler that returns (after writing to a pipe)
           runs the handler and is still terminated by SIGABRT; abort()
           does not return.
test       t/003-handler-returns.c

assertion  XSH.abort.004
anchor     functions/abort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A child whose SIGABRT handler leaves with siglongjmp() goes on after
           abort() is interrupted that way and exits normally.
test       t/004-handler-leaves.c

assertion  XSH.abort.005
anchor     functions/abort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       In a child where a second thread calls abort(), the SIGABRT handler
           runs in that thread (seen through a thread-local value set
           before), not in the main thread.
note       The handler reads a thread-local int last written before the
           signal and leaves with _exit(), both allowed in a handler.
test       t/005-calling-thread.c
